    "created_at": "2016-08-01T09:22:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-01T09:24:19Z",
    "body": "I do not have a strong opinion, however, +1 for \"A is potentially reachable from B\".\n\n I remember that I thought the similar wording. One concern is:\n\ne.g.\n\n```\nlet a = document.createElement(\"div\");\nlet b = document.createElement(\"div\");\n```\n\nIn this case, `a` is _unclosed node_ of `b`, and vice-versa. Thus, _reachable_ might not reflect the situation correctly.  They are _unreachable_ from each other, in terms of DOM APIs.\n\nMaybe it's okay. _Reachable_ might be better than mysterious _unclosed_, I think.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
